; A locative into the middle of an extra-pdl object is copied out with the
; object (sys/ucadr/uc-transporter.lisp, EXTRA-PDL-TRAP).  Load
; lisp/extra-pdl-interior.lisp first, interpreted or compiled.  Microcode that
; reads the copy's header at the locative's address, 2^63's second digit, 0,
; halts in ILLOP at SINF-FLO, and the case gets no answer.
;
; The control and preconditions: the bignum lies in the extra pdl, its digit
; reads the same through a locative, and the word is 0.
(epi-control 2097152) => (T T T)
; The locative stored into an array (EXTRA-PDL-TRAP from the write test).
(epi-store 2097152) => (T T T)
; The locative held across a stack-group switch (EXTRA-PDL-TRAP-0, from the
; pdl buffer's dump).
(epi-hold 2097152) => (T (T T T))
